  "full_sections_read": "PartI setup and entire2.1–2.2, entire3.1 and complete3.3–3.4; physical printed pages21–24,27–30,32–34. No entire-book read claim.",
  "bounded_primary_paraphrase": "Part I uses finite state and action sets and real stage costs. Section2.2 fixes discount0<alpha<1 and normalized discounted totals; Remark2.1 explains conversion to unnormalized totals. Theorem3.2 identifies every behavioral occupation vector with a stationary-policy vector and a compact finite polytope. Theorem3.3 supplies an optimal stationary policy from feasibility alone. Section3.3/Theorem3.6 exchanges the primal and dual extrema using compact convex occupation measures; its separate Slater discussion gives general multiplier attainment. Section3.4/Theorem3.7 presents the finite dual LP with a maximum and its value equality. Our separate actual finite-polytope Lean construction proves scalar multiplier attainment without assuming Slater; this is not attributed solely to Theorem3.6.",
  "normalization_correspondence": "Multiplication by the positive constant1-alpha converts the author normalization to the actual unnormalized Lean path returns. Finite source risk is scalar; max-reward/min-cost signs are exchanged explicitly by negation.",
  "attribution_limit": "Theorem3.6 alone is not said to guarantee a finite attained multiplier without Slater. Feasibility-alone attained finite scalar multiplier is genuinely constructed by the separate full8-source Lean result and reviewed independently.",
